<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/151cb3a9acf1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1098] A self-driving Lexus SUV owned by Google's parent company Alphabet struck a bus February 14 while it was testing on the streets of Mountain View, Calif." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1098" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1e689cbfe214> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1083] Google is to meet with California's Department of Motor Vehicles (DMV) to discuss the incident, and determine where the blame lies." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1083" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/28195dc0019f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1100] the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration—which regulates U.S. vehicle-safety standards—said earlier this month that it counts the artificial intelligence controlling Google’s cars as a “driver.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1100" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2b6b2659c01c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google car hits bus, first time at fault" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1098" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2eac190eef15> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The incident – which California’s Department of Motor Vehicles documented publicly yesterday – is the first clear-cut case of an accident caused by the tech giant’s self-driving technology." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1087" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/34e05b975c4d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration—which regulates U.S. vehicle-safety standards—said earlier this month that it counts the artificial intelligence controlling Google’s cars as a “driver.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1100" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3bc03982f0e6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Google's Self-Driving Car Hit Another Vehicle for the First Time" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1097" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/41ca75e397ad> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A public transit bus was approaching from behind. The Google AV test driver saw the bus approaching in the left side mirror but believed the bus would stop or slow to allow the Google AV to continue." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5250" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4c40e28571b4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "At SXSW, Urmson also showed an instance where a bike going the wrong way at night suddenly zoomed through an intersection, in front of a Google car, according to Gizmodo." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1082" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/579f3c777c8b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Newly released video shows the moment a Google self-driving car learned the hard way not to tussle with a public bus." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1106" .

