    airo:evidenceText "Google self-driving car caught on video colliding with bus" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1106" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/732bf894c488> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Google driverless car has been involved in an accident with a bus and Google has said it “bears some responsibility” for the first time." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1088" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7d247b495400> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "1 of Google’s autonomous Lexus SUVs hit a public bus on Valentine’s Day while trying to avoid sandbags on the road." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1100" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7dea30987534> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1095] On Valentine's Day, the inevitable happened to Google as one of its self-driving Lexuses was involved in a low-speed crash with a city bus." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1095" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/85bf3e12dfeb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[1082] 'Our car was making an assumption about what the other car was going to do,' said Chris Urmson, head of Google's self-driving project, speaking at the SXSW festival in Austin." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1082" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8c754e833700> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Urmson revealed the company had taught its cars to move next to the curb when planning a right turn, sidling by traffic stopped at a traffic light, much as human drivers do, according to CNET." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1082" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9f6cac2c7940> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Google self-driving car caused a crash for the first time" ;
